  "version": 1,
  "title": "Derivatives of Theta Functions and a Problem of Lyubarskii and Nes",
  "abstract": "Lean 4 formalization of the main result of the paper \"Derivatives of Theta Functions and a Problem of Lyubarskii and Nes\" by L. Liehr, I. Shafkulovska and M. A. Taylor (arXiv:2609.27846): if Λ = Mℤ² ⊂ ℝ² is a lattice of density D(Λ) = q/p, where p and q are coprime positive integers with q ≥ p + 2, then the Gabor system of the first Hermite function h₁(t) = t·exp(−πt²) along Λ is a frame for L²(ℝ).",
